    "2": {
      "html": "<h2>1 · Set Up</h2>\n<p class=\"cap\">Probe positions. Patient's right is on your left.</p>\n<p><b>Probe:</b> curvilinear, abdominal preset, depth ~16 cm. A phased array fits between ribs.</p>\n<p><b>Patient:</b> supine. If the GB hides: roll <b>left lateral decubitus</b>, deep breath and hold.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><b>Subcostal:</b> marker to head. Slide from the xiphoid along the right costal margin, aiming up under the ribs.</li>\n<li><b>X-7:</b> 7 cm from the xiphoid along the costal margin. A reliable start.</li>\n<li><b>Intercostal:</b> mid-axillary line (MAL), lower ribs. Liver is the window.</li>\n</ol>",
      "css": "font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\nfont-size: 9.5px;\nline-height: 1.28;\nh2 {\n  font-family: 'Silkscreen', monospace;\n  font-size: 12px;\n  border-bottom: 2px solid #000;\n  margin-bottom: 4px;\n}\np {\n  margin: 0 0 4px;\n}\nul, ol {\n  margin: 0 0 4px 13px;\n}\nli {\n  margin-bottom: 2px;\n}\n.auto-image {\n  border: 1px solid #000;\n  margin-bottom: 3px;\n}\n.cap {\n  font-size: 8px;\n  font-style: italic;\n  margin-bottom: 5px;\n}\n.pat-box > div {\n  padding: 4px;\n}",
      "image": "data:image/png;base64,",
      "imageMode": "threshold",
      "dotSize": 1,
      "columns": 1,
      "useMaster": true,
      "flow": false,
      "bg": 0
    },
    "3": {
      "html": "<h2>2 · Find It</h2>\n<p class=\"cap\">Normal GB. The main lobar fissure (MLF) runs from the portal vein to the neck: the \"exclamation point.\"</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Find the liver, then the <b>portal vein</b> (bright walls). Follow the <b>MLF</b> to the GB neck.</li>\n<li>GB: anechoic and pear-shaped, neck toward the porta, fundus anterior.</li>\n<li>Scan <b>long</b> and <b>short</b> axis, fanning through the whole GB in each plane. Stones hide in the neck.</li>\n<li>Normal wall <b>≤3 mm</b>; size up to ~10 × 4 cm.</li>\n<li>Mimics: IVC (deeper, collapses with breathing), duodenum (gas, peristalsis), renal cyst.</li>\n</ul>",
      "css": "font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\nfont-size: 9.5px;\nline-height: 1.28;\nh2 {\n  font-family: 'Silkscreen', monospace;\n  font-size: 12px;\n  border-bottom: 2px solid #000;\n  margin-bottom: 4px;\n}\np {\n  margin: 0 0 4px;\n}\nul, ol {\n  margin: 0 0 4px 13px;\n}\nli {\n  margin-bottom: 2px;\n}\n.auto-image {\n  border: 1px solid #000;\n  margin-bottom: 3px;\n}\n.cap {\n  font-size: 8px;\n  font-style: italic;\n  margin-bottom: 5px;\n}\n.pat-box > div {\n  padding: 4px;\n}",
      "image": "data:image/jpeg;base64,",
      "imageMode": "none",
      "dotSize": 1,
      "columns": 1,
      "useMaster": true,
      "flow": false,
      "bg": 0
    },
    "4": {
      "html": "<h2>3 · Stones</h2>\n<p class=\"cap\">Stone vs polyp: one shadows and falls, the other doesn't.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Stone:</b> bright focus + clean <b>posterior acoustic shadow</b> + <b>moves</b> when the patient rolls.</li>\n<li>Roll them or sit them up. A stone stuck in the neck that won't move is worrying.</li>\n<li><b>WES sign</b> (wall-echo-shadow): a contracted GB packed with stones. You see a bright arc and a shadow, but no lumen.</li>\n<li><b>Sludge:</b> layering low-level echoes, no shadow.</li>\n<li><b>Polyp:</b> fixed to the wall, no shadow.</li>\n<li>No shadow from a small stone? Put the focal zone at it and raise the frequency.</li>\n</ul>",
      "css": "font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\nfont-size: 9.5px;\nline-height: 1.28;\nh2 {\n  font-family: 'Silkscreen', monospace;\n  font-size: 12px;\n  border-bottom: 2px solid #000;\n  margin-bottom: 4px;\n}\np {\n  margin: 0 0 4px;\n}\nul, ol {\n  margin: 0 0 4px 13px;\n}\nli {\n  margin-bottom: 2px;\n}\n.auto-image {\n  border: 1px solid #000;\n  margin-bottom: 3px;\n}\n.cap {\n  font-size: 8px;\n  font-style: italic;\n  margin-bottom: 5px;\n}\n.pat-box > div {\n  padding: 4px;\n}",
      "image": "data:image/jpeg;base64,",
      "imageMode": "none",
      "dotSize": 1,
      "columns": 1,
      "useMaster": true,
      "flow": false,
      "bg": 0
    },
    "5": {
      "html": "<h2>4 · Cholecystitis</h2>\n<p class=\"cap\">Short axis: thick layered wall, pericholecystic fluid (PCF), stone. Measure the <i>anterior</i> wall.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Stones</b> (most acute cholecystitis is calculous)</li>\n<li><b>Sonographic Murphy:</b> worst pain with the probe right over the GB</li>\n<li><b>Anterior wall &gt;3 mm</b>, measured perpendicular. The posterior wall is blurred by enhancement.</li>\n<li><b>Pericholecystic fluid</b></li>\n<li><b>Distended:</b> &gt;4 cm transverse</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"pat-box pat-4\"><div><b>Stones + sonographic Murphy:</b> PPV ~92%. <b>Neither:</b> NPV ~95% (Ralls 1985).</div></div>",
      "css": "font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\nfont-size: 9.5px;\nline-height: 1.28;\nh2 {\n  font-family: 'Silkscreen', monospace;\n  font-size: 12px;\n  border-bottom: 2px solid #000;\n  margin-bottom: 4px;\n}\np {\n  margin: 0 0 4px;\n}\nul, ol {\n  margin: 0 0 4px 13px;\n}\nli {\n  margin-bottom: 2px;\n}\n.auto-image {\n  border: 1px solid #000;\n  margin-bottom: 3px;\n}\n.cap {\n  font-size: 8px;\n  font-style: italic;\n  margin-bottom: 5px;\n}\n.pat-box > div {\n  padding: 4px;\n}",
      "image": "data:image/jpeg;base64,",
      "imageMode": "none",
      "dotSize": 1,
      "columns": 1,
      "useMaster": true,
      "flow": false,
      "bg": 0
    },
    "6": {
      "html": "<h2>5 · The CBD</h2>\n<p class=\"cap\">\"Mickey Mouse\" at the porta hepatis: PV is the head; the CBD (patient's right) and hepatic artery (HA) are the ears.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Follow the MLF to the portal vein, then turn transverse to find Mickey.</li>\n<li><b>Color Doppler:</b> the CBD has no flow; the HA does.</li>\n<li>Measure <b>inner wall to inner wall</b>.</li>\n<li><b>Normal ≤6 mm.</b> Add ~1 mm per decade over 60. Up to ~10 mm after cholecystectomy.</li>\n<li>Dilated CBD + jaundice or fever: think choledocholithiasis or cholangitis.</li>\n</ul>",
      "css": "font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\nfont-size: 9.5px;\nline-height: 1.28;\nh2 {\n  font-family: 'Silkscreen', monospace;\n  font-size: 12px;\n  border-bottom: 2px solid #000;\n  margin-bottom: 4px;\n}\np {\n  margin: 0 0 4px;\n}\nul, ol {\n  margin: 0 0 4px 13px;\n}\nli {\n  margin-bottom: 2px;\n}\n.auto-image {\n  border: 1px solid #000;\n  margin-bottom: 3px;\n}\n.cap {\n  font-size: 8px;\n  font-style: italic;\n  margin-bottom: 5px;\n}\n.pat-box > div {\n  padding: 4px;\n}",
      "image": "data:image/jpeg;base64,",
      "imageMode": "none",
      "dotSize": 1,
      "columns": 1,
      "useMaster": true,
      "flow": false,
      "bg": 0
    },
    "7": {
      "html": "<h2>6 · Pitfalls</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Just ate?</b> A contracted GB looks thick-walled. Ask about the last meal.</li>\n<li><b>Thick wall ≠ cholecystitis.</b> Also CHF, ascites, cirrhosis, hepatitis, low albumin, pancreatitis, renal failure.</li>\n<li><b>Edge artifact:</b> a refraction shadow from the curved neck, with no bright focus in front. Not a stone.</li>\n<li><b>Duodenal gas</b> mimics a stone. Watch for peristalsis.</li>\n<li><b>Folds and septa</b> (Phrygian cap) are not stones. Fan through them.</li>\n<li><b>Murphy</b> is less reliable after opioids or with altered mental status. Don't withhold analgesia.</li>\n<li><b>Acalculous</b> cholecystitis: critically ill, no stones. Look anyway.</li>\n<li><b>Gas in the wall, sloughed membranes, asymmetric wall:</b> gangrenous or emphysematous. Call surgery.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"pat-box pat-9\"><div><b>POCUS rules in better than it rules out.</b> Negative scan but high suspicion: get a comprehensive RUQ ultrasound or HIDA.</div></div>",
      "css": "font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\nfont-size: 9.5px;\nline-height: 1.28;\nh2 {\n  font-family: 'Silkscreen', monospace;\n  font-size: 12px;\n  border-bottom: 2px solid #000;\n  margin-bottom: 4px;\n}\np {\n  margin: 0 0 4px;\n}\nul, ol {\n  margin: 0 0 4px 13px;\n}\nli {\n  margin-bottom: 2px;\n}\n.auto-image {\n  border: 1px solid #000;\n  margin-bottom: 3px;\n}\n.cap {\n  font-size: 8px;\n  font-style: italic;\n  margin-bottom: 5px;\n}\n.pat-box > div {\n  padding: 4px;\n}",
      "image": null,
      "imageMode": "none",
      "dotSize": 1,
      "columns": 1,
      "useMaster": true,
      "flow": false,
      "bg": 0
    },
    "8": {
      "html": "<h2>Checklist</h2>\n<p class=\"lead f-pixel\">Views</p>\n<ul class=\"cklist\">\n<li>GB long axis, fanned neck → fundus</li>\n<li>GB short axis, full sweep</li>\n<li>MLF traced to the portal vein</li>\n<li>Patient rolled (LLD): do stones move?</li>\n<li>Sonographic Murphy, probe on the GB</li>\n<li>CBD at the porta + color Doppler</li>\n<li>Morison's pouch and right kidney</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"lead f-pixel\">Measure</p>\n<table>\n<tr><td>Anterior wall</td><td>&gt;3 mm</td></tr>\n<tr><td>GB transverse</td><td>&gt;4 cm</td></tr>\n<tr><td>GB length</td><td>&gt;10 cm</td></tr>\n<tr><td>CBD, inner–inner</td><td>&gt;6 mm*</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p class=\"foot\">*+1 mm per decade over 60; ≤10 mm after cholecystectomy.</p>\n<p class=\"lead f-pixel\">Document</p>\n<p class=\"doc\">Stones Y/N · mobile Y/N · Murphy +/− · wall __ mm · PCF Y/N · CBD __ mm</p>\n<p class=\"foot\">Simulated images. Teaching aid: follow your local protocols.</p>",
      "css": "font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\nfont-size: 9.5px;\nline-height: 1.28;\nh2 {\n  font-family: 'Silkscreen', monospace;\n  font-size: 12px;\n  border-bottom: 2px solid #000;\n  margin-bottom: 4px;\n}\np {\n  margin: 0 0 4px;\n}\nul, ol {\n  margin: 0 0 4px 13px;\n}\nli {\n  margin-bottom: 2px;\n}\n.auto-image {\n  border: 1px solid #000;\n  margin-bottom: 3px;\n}\n.cap {\n  font-size: 8px;\n  font-style: italic;\n  margin-bottom: 5px;\n}\n.pat-box > div {\n  padding: 4px;\n}\n.lead {\n  font-size: 9px;\n  margin: 5px 0 2px;\n}\n.cklist {\n  list-style: none;\n  margin-left: 0;\n}\n.cklist li::before {\n  content: '☐ ';\n  font-size: 11px;\n}\ntable {\n  width: 100%;\n  border-collapse: collapse;\n}\ntd {\n  border: 1px solid #000;\n  padding: 1px 4px;\n}\ntd:last-child {\n  text-align: right;\n  font-weight: bold;\n}\n.foot {\n  font-size: 7.5px;\n  font-style: italic;\n  margin-top: 2px;\n}\n.doc {\n  border: 1px dashed #000;\n  padding: 3px;\n}",
